84" :question/math-academy-id "q-23799" :question/problem "$\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta } & =\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta (1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )}{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we rewrite the numerator using $1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta $ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta (1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )}{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta } & =\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }}{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we rewrite $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta $ using its definition and simplify further:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{2\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }}\\cdot \\frac{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }=\\frac{1}{2}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-23799/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "23637774-8d69-500d-8cb0-5e41a0207542"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-23799"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-65230/selection/4a5e918ea312eced90c9c1cddfd857ab09d00da4fbc89b8bc177ba3dc139a14b" :answer/id #uuid "cdae2963-3f49-5581-8d07-496462e34261" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65230/selection/54661d432eed36afb6f5a8d712e4546a08ef08094e547d421ed7e6f15b72dad8" :answer/id #uuid "19bb7ca2-8721-569a-85c9-30faad1d7076" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65230/selection/81d31a2e82f9c3ee5b2bc61d0410bfbabe8d187f8c5fc792d56fa77ce9aecc9a" :answer/id #uuid "45278438-d5a7-504c-9a31-4c8cf5453455" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65230/selection/35c0d04af9622de3840be4b9057e0e217b5b397382260d5721b234450e0a3153" :answer/id #uuid "2f0e58ff-5474-5224-94e3-4abd401f7c30" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65230/selection/9f5d6ebc37e3e9c474831c3dab83213664bb8cf4a3a0293e6f1120f4e65ce5bb" :answer/id #uuid "ec66259c-8018-5545-a8f1-c5caecf8bb93" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65230/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b247076c-c1ac-5479-a608-edf44d31b8da" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-65230/selection/54661d432eed36afb6f5a8d712e4546a08ef08094e547d421ed7e6f15b72dad8" :answer-field/choices ["q-65230/selection/4a5e918ea312eced90c9c1cddfd857ab09d00da4fbc89b8bc177ba3dc139a14b" "q-65230/selection/54661d432eed36afb6f5a8d712e4546a08ef08094e547d421ed7e6f15b72dad8" "q-65230/selection/81d31a2e82f9c3ee5b2bc61d0410bfbabe8d187f8c5fc792d56fa77ce9aecc9a" "q-65230/selection/35c0d04af9622de3840be4b9057e0e217b5b397382260d5721b234450e0a3153" "q-65230/selection/9f5d6ebc37e3e9c474831c3dab83213664bb8cf4a3a0293e6f1120f4e65ce5bb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-65230" :question/id #uuid "34fb018a-fb92-5d81-97f5-ac350e3ba4c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-65230" :question/problem "Simplify the expression $\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the numerator using $1-{cos}^{2}⁡x={sin}^{2}⁡x.$\n\n$$\n\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1}=\\frac{1-{cos}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1}\n$$\n\nNext, we factor the numerator as a difference of squares, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1-{cos}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1} & =\\frac{(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{1} \\\\  & =1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-65230/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b05f4be1-95d4-5137-bbaa-71c95862bb59"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-65230"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-65231/selection/369ba9ff644b2a3c7078acbd6fa5be77cdac2f7173cade671df5c75448a99d4f" :answer/id #uuid "7f4ef61b-bc65-5764-9680-29afdfd7b0f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1+{sin}^{2}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-