denominator using $1-{sin}^{2}⁡x={cos}^{2}⁡x.$\n\n$$\n\\frac{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}=\\frac{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{1-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\n$$\n\nNext, we factor the denominator as difference of squares, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{1-{sin}^{2}⁡x} & =\\frac{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}}{\\cancel{(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)}(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-65231/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b05f4be1-95d4-5137-bbaa-71c95862bb59"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-65231"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-119863/selection/7048515d8d03871e88488698b26c9b226ee04b8b8095a0a53e3c45f7964a4c43" :answer/id #uuid "85354926-9425-5e53-b0a4-57f3c8ba1349" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119863/selection/03de4263b01227d38ca1bbc571c37b90a631ff72dd37de9e5ea86d66053f7547" :answer/id #uuid "8f074cf0-d381-52e4-90e9-d74cab79631e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119863/selection/29be3cf1aa7619e3ab92ed63e9016b4012bc96ee45049581d3b9397c2783490c" :answer/id #uuid "e5017409-f15c-5adb-8dd5-6c9a61279f0f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119863/selection/ff8f1ffdc2cbfb1a4a64c41b9ac9f0be14fabc5b524807351f2d1cd1f9f0e487" :answer/id #uuid "d4206203-dd0a-51cb-9924-bc39b08707e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119863/selection/ea1e338de2a0cb8a640a44950398210d1ca222223a655996523a7e9a1815ad8e" :answer/id #uuid 