d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-119867" :question/id #uuid "414f60cd-2190-52c9-a257-e6caaf96811e" :question/math-academy-id "q-119867" :question/problem "Simplify $\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the numerator of the first term using $1-{sin}^{2}⁡x={cos}^{2}⁡x.$\n\n$$\n\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=\\frac{1-{sin}^{2}⁡x}{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\n$$\n\nNext, we factor the numerator of the first term as a difference of squares, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1-{sin}^{2}⁡x}{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =\\frac{(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)}{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)}(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)}{\\cancel{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\  & =\\frac{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{1}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\  & =1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-119867/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b05f4be1-95d4-5137-bbaa-71c95862bb59"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-119867"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
